The Claude Code and Codex reproduction suites are twins: each installs a physical copy of the package sources into a shared install and compiles the same hook from checkouts at different nesting depths, asserting byte-identical output and a checkout-anchored runtime import. Scenarios added to one twin must be mirrored in the other, because the two agent compile paths share the wrapper-generation logic these suites pin.
